From afd305e58c6f4d3f223e9c7a8b98c363641d4d7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:21:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: asynchronous evaluation of the material
 properties

As the integration of the behaviours, the evaluation of the material
properties may be synchronous or asynchronous, on all the backends:

- the execution options take the statuses of an asynchronous evaluation
  (`statuses`, array of `<name>_generic_parallel_number_of_statuses`
  integers initialized to zero by the calling code). If they are given,
  the function returns once the computations are submitted to the queue
  (CUDA, HIP, Kokkos, SYCL if no value is copied) and only reports invalid
  arguments and runtime errors;
- the analysis of the statuses is generated once, in an exported function
  (`<name>_generic_parallel_report`), called by the synchronous
  evaluations and by the calling code once the computations of an
  asynchronous evaluation are completed. The kernels are unchanged: they
  only write the statuses when a bound is violated or when a result is
  invalid.

Tests on all the backends: asynchronous evaluation with a temperature out
of its physical bounds, reported after synchronization; with CUDA and HIP,
the stream is still busy when the function returns (a kernel writing the
arguments after a delay precedes the evaluation).
